      },
      "body": "`BufferQueue.get()` removes consumed groups from `data` but leaves their `group_timestamps` entries behind. Repeated write/read cycles therefore retain every consumed instance ID and timestamp.\n\nRemove the matching timestamp after the existing successful data removal. Incomplete groups and a group whose transformation raises retain their data and timestamp.\n\nThe regression tests exercise the real FastAPI write/read routes, incomplete groups, reused IDs and transformation errors. The new test is registered in the CPU workflow matrix, with FastAPI/uvicorn installed only for that test; the generated workflow is included.\n\nValidation on macOS / Python 3.13:\n- The same regression tests: base **3 failed, 1 passed**; this change **4 passed**.\n- Independent CPU/ASGI review checks, including a concurrent same-ID write: **5 passed**.\n- Ruff and `git diff --check` passed; generated workflow matches its template.\n\nThese checks cover this CPU queue/ASGI path. Distributed Ray/GPU training and the upstream Python 3.10 CI lane have not been run locally.\n",
